Revision history for CAPE-Utils

5.0.?   ?/?
        - pod cleanup
        - no longer uses shortened md5 in suricata_extract_submit but full sha1
        - add $ENV{MOJO_CAPE_SUBMIT_MAX_REQ_SIZE} for controlling max request size for mojo_cape_submit
        - fix handling of MOJO_CAPE_SUBMIT_MAX_REQ_SIZE
        - fix handling of printing received info in the log for mojo_cape_submit
        - add a incrementing int to mojo_cape_submit logging so log entries can more easily be corolated
        - mojo_cape_submit renamed to nergal and broken out into CAPE::Utils::Nergal
        - add a mojo_cape_submit wrapper that maps MOJO_CAPE_SUBMIT_MAX_REQ_SIZE to NERGAL_MAX_REQ_SIZE
          and execs nergal, for anything still calling it by the old name
        - add a nergal results endpoint (GET /results/<task_id> and /results/<task_id>/<file>) for
          fetching detonation artifacts
        - add a systemd timer for running cape_utils eve every two minutes
        - eve now writes per-task JSONs under the incoming dir's eve/ subdir and reads incoming JSON via
          task_to_json; drop the dead incoming_json config setting
        - fix check_remote ACL logic: ip/apikey/both/either now behave correctly (previously a bare apikey
          bypassed the IP check and ip-only auth denied keyless requests)
        - add a cape_utils exec command for running an arbitrary command from the CAPE base dir via
          poetry, the same way submissions are executed
        - submit and exec now require being ran as the configured cape_runas user (default cape); when not,
          they prepend "sudo -u <cape_runas>" if enable_sudo is set (defaults to 1 when ran as root,
          otherwise 0) or die
        - nergal now recovers the flow info, slug, pre send sha1, extraction time, and mime from the submitted
          filename when it is in the standard <src_ip>-<src_port>-<dest_ip>-<dest_port>-<proto>-<sha1>-<slug>-<epoch>-<mime>
          format, for the sake of tools submitting in that format without the JSON body suricata_extract_submit sends;
          every field is validated, matching is all or nothing, the epoch is taken as UTC, and anything actually
          submitted always wins
        - nergal now uses only the file bit of the submitted filename, which previously had just its first '/' stripped,
          letting a submitter walk out of the incoming dir and have the JSON write, the unlink, and the symlink all land
          on an arbitrary path; the name as submitted is still recorded as .cape_submit.orig_name and resub got the same
          treatment
        - nergal no longer autovivifies empty http, suricata_extract_submit, and lilith_cape_submit sections into every
          incoming JSON it writes out
        - nergal now ignores a json param that does not decode to a hash instead of failing the submission with a 400
        - nergal_extend now buckets submissions with no slug under 'unknown' rather than an
          empty string, which also silences the uninitialized value warnings it emitted for them
        - add a submission_gate config value for nergal, a command ran per submission that decides what becomes of it
          via how it exits; 0 accepts, 1 accepts and saves without submitting, 2 accepts and keeps nothing, 3/4/5 deny
          with a 444/445/403, and anything else, a gate that cannot be ran, or one that runs past submission_gate_timeout
          is an error and drops the submission. The submission is described to it via NERGAL_ prefixed env vars and its
          stdout, stderr, and exit are logged and recorded as .cape_submit.gate_results
        - nergal_extend now detects a changed hash via the digest in the name when the submitter sent no sha256,
          so submissions without a suricata_extract_submit section are no longer all counted as changed; that digest
          is a full sha1 from current submitters but the first 18 characters of the md5 from older ones, so it is
          compared as a prefix against both the sha1 and the md5 taken on receipt
        - add mime based package selection for submit via mime_to_package, off by default
        - add the mime_packages config section, mapping mime types to CAPE packages
        - add cape_utils submit --mime-package and --dry-run
        - add cape_utils mime_to_packages for printing the mime to package settings, with --as-ini
          and --diff for printing them as INI and limiting it to what differs from the defaults
        - get_tasks_count now adds the "where" keyword when the passed where does not already start
          with it, so cape_utils tasks -C -w takes the same string as cape_utils tasks -w instead of
          building invalid SQL
        - document the exec, poetry, resub, and mime_to_packages commands in the cape_utils POD, fix
          post's entry to take a run ID rather than a report JSON, and point the per command links at
          the CAPE::Utils methods backing them rather than the POD-less command modules
        - remove search, a old unimplemented feature
        - fix cape_utils post handing the INI path to its cape_utils helper instead of the options
          hash ref, which made post -i die
        - document the internal subs and the App::Cmd command classes, add a from source install
          section to the README, and drop the duplicate AUTHOR section from CAPE::Utils::LogDrek
        - submit now actually shuffles when "random" is set, which it documented but never did; the
          items read out of a submitted dir are shuffled in with the rest rather than kept together
        - drop the submit "custom" option, which submit() never implemented and nothing else, the
          POD entry aside, existed for
        - document post_link_format_template and post_link_format_template_file in the CONFIG FILE
          section, both having been in the defaults but not the docs
        - fix the suricata_extract_submit config docs: the UA ignore key is ignoreUA and not
          ignoreUAs, ignoreHosts was listed twice, and ignoreMaxSize is a byte limit rather than
          the file of regexes its comment claimed
        - fix suricata_extract_submit_extend -c, -d, and -r, which were declared to GetOptions as
          bare booleans, so passing any of them a value set it to 1 and left the value in @ARGV
        - cape_utils version now reports the CAPE::Utils version rather than the CAPE::Utils::Cmd
          App::Cmd glue version, which was stuck at 0.1.0 and said nothing about what it can do
        - document submission_gate and submission_gate_timeout in the CONFIG FILE section, and bring
          both README config blocks back in step with the PODs they mirror, the CAPE::Utils one
          having been missing 13 settings and the suricata_extract_submit one 8
        - the README now says what the six installed scripts are, introduces the cape_utils CLI and
          its sub commands, and covers nergal_extend and suricata_extract_submit_extend
        - fix the nergal ping test docs, which said a size 10 file matching /01234567890/ when that
          is 11 bytes and so could never match... it is /1234567890/, and the log line said the same
          wrong payload
        - nergal now creates the incoming sub dirs at start up via CAPE::Utils::Nergal->make_dirs,
          rather than refusing every submission until they were made by hand; the incoming dir
          itself is still never created, as it is normally a mount
        - nergal can now write HTTP access logs under the incoming dir's http_access_logs sub dir
          via the optional module Mojolicious::Plugin::AccessLog, enabled via enable_access_logs,
          which defaults to 0; rotated daily, written as access-<YYYY-MM-DD>.log in combinedio format
        - nergal now defaults MOJO_MODE to production instead of Mojolicious' development, so a
          request it has no route for is no longer replied to with a page listing every route, the
          request internals, and the module versions; MOJO_MODE, PLACK_ENV, and -m still win, this
          mattering most for CGI, where there is no command line to pass -m on
        - nergal now answers a GET of a submission URL with a 405 and an Allow of POST, rather than
          a 404 that reads like the URL is wrong when the method was the only thing that was

4.0.0   2025-07-21/15:00
        - Add poetry_path config with a default of /etc/poetry/bin/poetry, which is where it is located for new CAPEv2 installs... older installs should set it to just poetry

3.0.0   2024-09-24/16:30
        - Add ignoreMaxSize with a default value of 52428800 for skipping large extracts.

2.9.0   2024-08-01/16:20
        - Remove unused depend on YAML. Thanks @perlpunk in issues/2.
        - Add support for ignoring stuff using Web::ACL.
        - Add ignore support for paths and UAs via a file of regexs

2.8.0   2023-11-27/11:00
        - convert to Pod::Usage
        - replace CryptX with cli utils

2.7.1   2023-11-15/10:00
        - fix tempdir cleanup

2.7.0   2023-06-18/19:30
        - doc cleanup for suricata_extract_submit_extend
        - mojo_cape_submit_extend doc update and now update app protos and max size

2.6.0   2023-06-14/21:15
        - add mojo_cape_submit_extend
        - Fix sub_size for suricata_extract_submit

2.5.0   2023-06-12/14:00
       - suricata_extract_submit and extend now tracks submitted byte size
       - suricata_extract_submit now uses Proc::PID::File to make sure only one instance is running

2.4.0   2023-06-03/15:15
        - Add report munging support.

2.3.0   2023-05-18/18:00
        - suricata_extract_submit can now use env specified proxies optionally
        - suricata_extract_submit_extend now recomputes deltas

2.2.2   2023-05-18/10:00
        - Fix pod error in Utils.pm, reneeb PR#1
        - Set extend version to 1 in returned JSON.

2.2.1   2023-05-17/15:00
        - Actually reset last_errors post loading the old stats JSON

2.2.0   2023-05-17/12:00
        - cpanratings.perl.org no longer exists(147814)
        - src_bin/suricata_extract_submit now properly adds slug to the submission section
        - src_bin/suricata_extract_submit now tracks truncated files count

2.1.0   2023-05-17/09:45
        - Update logging for ignored items to be more verbose.

2.0.0   2023-05-16/16:00
        - Add CAPE::Utils->eve_process and matching eve command to cape_utils.
        - suricata_extract_submit now creates a stats file at '/var/cache/suricata_extract_submit_stats.json'.
        - suricata_extract_submit also sends stats to syslog
        - suricata_extract_submit sends the full extract JSON and mojo_cape_submit saves it.
        - Add src_bin/suricata_extract_submit_extend.

1.0.1   2023-03-30/20:00
        - Fix a typo in regards to regex loading for ignore hosts regex file

1.0.0   2023-03-30/16:15
        - Rework the auth system. Not backwards compatabile.
        - Add ignoreHosts options for ignoring hosts via regexp for suricata_extract_submit

0.1.0   2023-03-23/18:15
        - Add json output to -a submit
        - submit now returns a hash of submitted files and task IDs
        - add src_bin/mojo_cape_submit
        - add src_bin/suricata_extract_submit

0.0.1   2023-03-11/11:00
        - Initial version.
